top gun maverick the action-packed  dogfighting thriller starring tom cruise  recently set its place as one of the  highest grossing films of all time  bringing in over 1.3 billion dollars  worldwide and this might actually be  impressive too  if it wasn't stolen  from star wars people seem to love top  gun maverick and it certainly shows in  the critical response with a certified  fresh 96 rotten tomatoes score and  record-breaking box office numbers when  i saw the film i loved it too but i  couldn't help but notice the fact that  they completely ripped off the story  from the original star wars  roll the intro  [Music]  before we get started here's a spoiler  warning for top gun maverick we will be  talking about lots of spoilers in the  film so please wait to watch this video  until after you've seen it if you don't  want it to be spoiled in this video  we're going to go over how top gun  directly copied star wars down to the  plot characters and mission as well as  why it was so successful even as a  complete rip-off in essence i'll explain  how top gun maverick stole 1.3 billion  dollars by copying star wars but first i  want to say that i love star wars so  it's no coincidence that i also really  love top gun maverick and i'm not just  saying that because of its similarities  to star wars the film actually had a  fantastic story with great character  development and high stakes throughout  the entire movie one of the biggest  things that stuck out to me though was  no not miles teller's mustache no what  stuck out to me was the great attention  to detail tom cruise is known for doing  all of his own stunts so it should come  as no surprise that every dogfight scene  was filmed in actual f-18 fighter jets  that means no green screens and no cgi  the actors actually had to train their  bodies to prep for the forces they would  undergo in the f-18s tom cruise wanted  to make sure his fellow actors were  ready for the experience of flying in  the high caliber fighter jets seen in  the movie so he put them through a sort  of boot camp before filming commenced  according to miles teller we were all  mini toms making this movie he put us  through i'll just call it a tom cruise  boot camp we were getting in killer  shape and also for the stunts and stuff  that tom does in movies it's usually a  very specific type of training you're  not just going into the gym and lifting  some weights we did flight training for  three months before we started filming  we got put through the ringer they even  underwent training in an apparatus known  as the dunker where the trainee is  blindfolded and dunked underwater before  being spun around where they have to  find their way out it's this kind of  training and level of attention to  detail that really sold the movie for me  and for many other people too but i  still couldn't get over the pretty  blatant star wars imitation throughout  the film for starters the characters in  star wars and new hope and top gun  maverick are eerily similar they both  feature a young male protagonist whose  father died when they were children with  rooster as the protagonist and top gun  and luke skywalker as the protagonist in  star wars they're both watched over by  an older man who eventually trains them  this mentor was also best friends with  their father and can be found in the  characters of maverick and obi-wan  kenobi in each of the stories the  protagonist wants to follow in their  father's footsteps and they become one  of the best pilots in the world or the  galaxy later in the film they're engaged  in a super dangerous mission to destroy  an enemy weapon of mass destruction  whether it be a uranium refining  facility or a world killing death star  their missions both entail a low  altitude high speed trench run made in  an effort to avoid anti-aircraft weapons  both have to hit a small ventilation  shaft but i will say that we found our  first difference between the two movies  because rooster's ventilation shaft is 3  meters wide while luke's was just 2  meters wide before taking their final  victory shots both main characters hear  their mentor speak to them telling them  don't think just feel or to use the  force and trust your feelings which is  basically the same thing so they both  take their final shots with no guidance  technology and save the day lastly the  film's arrogant pilot hangman and han  solo comes in at the last minute to  shoot down the final enemy pilot and  saves the main character the number of  similarities between these two films and  their plots is astounding also just look  at how similar tie fighter pilot helmets  look to the top gun helmets i mean come  on with all of these similarities it  seems pretty obvious that top gun  maverick is a direct replication of star  wars a new hope the film's director  joseph kaczynski even said i think when  jerry bruckheimer made top gun star wars  was definitely an inspiration for them  so it makes sense that dna would carry  into ours so how exactly are they able  to get away with directly copying star  wars when their director is even saying  that's exactly what they did and the  answer because it's actually a really  good movie probably one of the best of  tom cruise's entire career it had an  exceptional cast great writing a  well-executed series of character arcs a  high attention to detail and it reminded  people of one of the best movies of all  time star wars while it's certainly not  the type of movie you think of for a  revival of the original star wars the  creators of top gun maverick still did  an exceptional job putting it all  together it's honestly kind of a miracle  that the movie exists and it's a miracle  it's as good as it is top gun maverick  is a sequel to a misty-eyed campy 80s  action movie that didn't really warrant  a sequel it's been 35 years now since  the release of the original top gun and  i don't think anyone was expecting that  we'd see tom cruise in the cockpit on  the silver screen ever again but here we  are with tom cruise at almost 60 years  old it's shocking to see him flying  under the immense pressure of an f-18  but then again we've seen him do crazier  things in his mission impossible movies  including flying through the sky  attached to the side of a world war ii  aircraft and holding his breath for over  six minutes while filming a scene  underwater  he truly is a fantastic actor with a  high level of dedication to his work and  it certainly shows in top gun maverick  regardless of whether the movie took  some pretty heavy inspiration from star  wars but i'd like to know what you think  how much do you think top gun maverick  took from star wars drop your thoughts  in the comment section below also check  out the video on your screen for some  more of my content don't forget to like  and subscribe and thanks for watching  rocket riley  [Music]
 

